From: Revive PSG1 build preparation
Subject: [LOCAL BUILD ONLY] Bound Soong primary-builder memory

The Android 15 Soong graph process exceeded a 24 GiB Docker VM limit under
Rosetta. Go 1.23 supports GOMEMLIMIT, so keep the graph builder below 20 GiB
and leave headroom for the VM, Ninja, and the Docker control plane.

This changes build-tool garbage-collection behavior only. It does not alter
target source, packages, properties, signing, or generated Android contents.

diff --git a/ui/build/soong.go b/ui/build/soong.go
--- a/ui/build/soong.go
+++ b/ui/build/soong.go
@@ -213,5 +213,8 @@ func (pb PrimaryBuilderFactory) primaryBuilderInvocation(config Config) bootstra
 	commonArgs = append(commonArgs, "-l", filepath.Join(pb.config.FileListDir(), "Android.bp.list"))
 	invocationEnv := make(map[string]string)
+	// Local build-host constraint; Go 1.23 treats this as a soft runtime limit.
+	// Keep enough VM headroom for Ninja and Docker while generating the graph.
+	invocationEnv["GOMEMLIMIT"] = "20GiB"
 	if pb.debugPort != "" {
 		//debug mode
 		commonArgs = append(commonArgs, "--delve_listen", pb.debugPort,
